+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+if [[ $# -lt 2 ]]; then
+  echo "usage: $0 LOG_PATH COMMAND [ARG ...]" >&2
+  exit 64
+fi
+
+log_path=$1
+shift
+
+{
+  printf 'WORKDIR: %q\n' "$PWD"
+  printf 'COMMAND:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+} >"$log_path"
+
+"$@" >>"$log_path" 2>&1
+status=$?
+
+printf 'EXIT_STATUS: %d\n' "$status" >>"$log_path"
+exit "$status"

codex
The separate entry-only command removes the `scan-loop` helper from the active specification and therefore keeps unrolling a symbolic list; after more than three minutes it still has no result. That run is diagnostic, not the candidate’s positive command. I’m stopping it and relying on the fresh full-spec run—which independently executed both positive claims together, as the proof is designed to do—plus the separate successful helper-claim run.
